  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State obligated $6.9B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of State made 20,114 awards with an average award size of $342K. Obligations fell 30.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a peak at $12B in FY22, then a decline to $9.8B in FY25 and $6.9B in FY26. The largest spending categories in FY2026 to date are Computer Systems Design Services with $813M, Security Guards and Patrol Services with $812M, and Other Computer Related Services with $767M. Construction, consulting, facilities, and banking services also appear among the top categories. The top vendors in FY2026 to date include CADDELL CONSTRUCTION CO. (DE), LLC with $524M, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $283M, and CGI FEDERAL INC. with $240M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has State's contract spending changed year to year?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $6.9B in FY26 to date compared with $9.8B in FY25. The Department of State obligations reached $12B in FY22 and were $11.7B in both FY23 and FY24. The Department of State obligations fell 30.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What industries and vendors receive the most State contract dollars?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services, Security Guards and Patrol Services, and Other Computer Related Services are the top three categories with $813M, $812M, and $767M respectively. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services follow with $570M and $488M. CADDELL CONSTRUCTION CO. (DE), LLC, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC., and CGI FEDERAL INC. are the top three vendors with $524M, $283M, and $240M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
